stom"],["Chrysostom: Homilies on Galatians to Philemon"]],[12009034,1,["Chrysostom"],["Chrysostom: Homilies on Galatians to Philemon"]]],"f":[["Chrysostom",6,["Homilies on Galatians to Philemon","Homilies on John and Hebrews","Homilies on Matthew"],"Would you learn how much prayers have profited? consider, I pray, Cornelius, Tabitha. (Acts x. 3 and ix. 36.) Hear also Jacob saying to Laban, \"Except the Fear of my father had been with me, surely thou hadst now sent me away empty.\" (Gen. xxxi. 42.) Hear also God again, saying,"],["Augustine",4,["Answer to Letters of Petilian","Letters","On the Merits and Forgiveness of Sins"],"241.  Augustin answered:  I seemed too a little while ago, when we were disputing about the oil of the sinner, to anoint your forehead, in order that you might say, if you dared, whether you yourself were not a sinner.  You have had the hardihood to say as much.  What a portentou"],["Gregory Nazianzen",2,["In Defence of His Flight to Pontus (Oration II)","Select Orations"],"89.  Who will cry aloud, Spare Thy People, O Lord, and give not Thine heritage to reproach, that the nations should rule over them?  What Noah, and Job,  and Daniel, who are reckoned together as men of prayer, will pray for us, that we may have a slight respite from warfare, and"],["Apostolic",1,["The Homily"]],["Clement Rome",1,["The Second Epistle of Clement"]],["Jerome",1,["Against Jovinianus"]]]},"15":{"l":[[43005029,6.0,"c",["G5337","G2222"]],[42016025,5.8,"c",["G2556","G2222"]],[60003010,5.8,"c",["G2556","G2222"]],[60004003,5.2,"c",["G979","G3928"]],[66017016,4.7,"c",["G2049","G2342"]],[54005005,4.5,"c",["G3443"]],[44028005,4.5,"c",["G2556","G2342"]],[56001012,4.5,"c",["G2556","G2342"]],[26005017,19.1,"s",["H7921","H2416","H5674","H7451"]],[3026006,12.2,"s",["H2416","H5674","H7451"]],[3026022,11.1,"s",["H7921","H2416"]],[18021010,11.0,"s",["H7921","H5674"]],[12002019,10.8,"s",["H7921","H7451"]],[2023029,10.6,"s",["H8077","H2416"]],[36002009,10.6,"s",["H8077","H2416"]],